SGX530: layers of at least 16x16 pixels

The N9's SGX530 reports framebuffers smaller than 16x16 as incomplete, "missing attachment"
and "Unsupported framebuffer format": FastBlur, whose last levels are 8, 4... pixels, drew
nothing. Their textures are rendered at 16 pixels instead.

--- a/src/quick/scenegraph/qsgopengllayer.cpp
+++ b/src/quick/scenegraph/qsgopengllayer.cpp
@@ -225,8 +225,12 @@
     markDirtyTexture();
 }
 
-void QSGOpenGLLayer::setSize(const QSize &size)
+void QSGOpenGLLayer::setSize(const QSize &pixelSize)
 {
+    // Harmattan (SGX530): framebuffers under 16x16 are incomplete ("Unsupported framebuffer
+    // format"), and FastBlur's smallest levels drew nothing. They are rendered at 16 pixels:
+    // the texture is sampled in normalized coordinates, so only its resolution changes.
+    const QSize size = pixelSize.isEmpty() ? pixelSize : pixelSize.expandedTo(QSize(16, 16));
     if (size == m_size)
         return;
     m_size = size;
